        "sequence": "$WEZTERM_PANE, $WEZTERM_EXECUTABLE",
        "description": "WezTerm sets a family of <code>WEZTERM_*</code> environment variables in every spawned shell. <code>WEZTERM_PANE</code> contains the numeric pane ID, <code>WEZTERM_EXECUTABLE</code> points at the wezterm binary, and additional variables expose the config directory and unix socket used by the <code>wezterm cli</code> tool.\n\nApplications can detect a WezTerm session by checking for these variables, and the wezterm CLI uses them to target the correct pane when invoked from within the terminal.",
