        "description": "The <code>WT_SESSION</code> environment variable is set by Windows Terminal to a GUID that uniquely identifies the current terminal session. A companion variable, <code>WT_PROFILE_ID</code>, identifies the Windows Terminal profile that launched the shell.\n\nApplications use <code>WT_SESSION</code> as the canonical way to detect Windows Terminal, since older versions did not set <code>TERM_PROGRAM</code> and the <code>TERM</code> value on Windows is typically inherited from the underlying console host rather than chosen by Windows Terminal itself.",
